For orthogonal projection, the resulting vector must be collinear with the original vector $\mathbf{w}$, thus we will end up with a scalar multiple of $\mathbf{w}$.
\begin{align*}
\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} &= \frac{\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{w}}{\|\mathbf{w}\|^2} \mathbf{w}\\
\implies \|\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v}\| &= \left\|\frac{\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{w}}{\|\mathbf{w}\|^2} \mathbf{w}\right\| \\
&= \frac{|\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{w}|}{\|\mathbf{w}\|^2} \|\mathbf{w}\|\\
&= \frac{|\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{w}|}{\|\mathbf{w}\|}\\
&= \boxed{\frac{10}{7}}
\end{align*}

